# Version Rollover Rule

When updating app version strings (title, asset query params, visible version labels), use this rollover convention:

- Version format is `major.minor.patch`.
- Patch is base-10 rollover into minor.
- Example: `0.0.11` must be written as `0.1.1`.
- Equivalent carry rule: `minor += floor(patch / 10)`, `patch = patch % 10`.
- If minor reaches 10+, carry to major using the same base-10 logic.

Before finalizing a version bump, normalize the version to this convention in all version references.
